{
  "$comment": "Chapter 4 level 36. Idea: the mountain is a neutral hazard that hurts everyone, and the prize sits inside its reach. A green valley with a smoking cone east of the player; the summit cone (aboveSea 440) is impassable, so the only land route to the sneaky rival is the south pass at the cone foot (the north strait is water a player can fill with Raise Land). Stage 1 grow to 25 followers while 4 warden raiders come through the pass every 120 s from minute 9 (until 0, so an idle village falls near tick 15000). Stage 2 wakes the dormant flank ley stone, which starts the mountain: two 270 s clocks cast Volcano as tribe -1 just uphill of the stone (gaps of 130 s and 140 s), each warned 10 s before (message plus the hazardWarn ring) and followed 45 s later by a shape that slumps the crater back into the terrace so the stone stays walkable; rival priests (3 wardens, every 90 s) walk into the same fire. Hold the stone 120 s. Stage 3 unlocks the Watchtower; a one shot war band (8 wardens, 2 firecallers) marches 45 s later. Stage 4 burn the rival Hearth (12 wardens, 4 firecallers posted, 3 towers, maxTroops 8, maxPopulation 28, worshipAfterSeconds 3600 so it never races the player). All eruptions, raids and warnings are bounded by until. Measured with the hard aggressive bot at offset 2: stages done at ticks 4745, 8185, 9685, 15005 (offsets 0 to 3 win between about 13500 and 17500). Time limit 1800 s (36000 ticks).",
